-- `invalid_entry_export` for `flush` (boundary.md §9.12 (c), amended
-- 2026-10-21): the hoisted release file re-exports the runtime's `flush`
-- when the build keeps it (backend.md §15.11), and a module that exports one
-- name twice does not load, so `flush` is refused always, as `default` is,
-- the same in both builds. `stop` is listable: only a runtime module
-- supplies it, and the exports mode refuses a runtime module. One
-- diagnostic, for `flush`, against the project's manifest; nothing written.
